WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.890
You've reached the end of the gallery.

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.050
Let's walk back through it.

3
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.550
Landscapes made the continent look empty.

4
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.650
Portraits made Native people look timeless,
outside history.

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.910
Settler paintings made white Americans look
like the rightful heirs.

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.130
Remington carried the same visual grammar
from Wyoming to Cuba.

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.410
And Curtis gave the whole system a name:
The Vanishing Race.

8
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.470
But the people
in these pictures did not vanish.

9
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.080
Today there are more than five hundred seventy
federally recognized tribal nations

10
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.590
in the United States.

11
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.410
Images shape what people can imagine,
and imagination shapes history.

12
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:43.440
So the next time a picture feels simply true,
pause, and ask: who made it,

13
00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:45.750
and what does it want me to believe?
